preConditionHook:
// CLEARING THE PRIOR SWING POINT. The close is above the most
// recent CONFIRMED swing high by at least marginTicks; the short mirrors below
// the most recent swing low. At swingPointsCleared > 1 the close must be
// beyond that MANY of the recent same-side pivots, which is Brooks's "it
// reverses many bars, swing highs and bear flags of the prior trend" -- a
// strength reading, not a different pattern, so it is this rule at a larger
// count and not a second rule. At 1 it degenerates to the plain break of the
// last pivot.
//
// THE SCAN IS HAND-ROLLED IN BOTH TWINS, not a deeper SwingHigh occurrence:
// the count can exceed two and OCCURRENCE 3+ IS UNMEASURED in the register, so
// the pivots are found by the scan SwingPivotTarget uses rather than by
// occurrence calls. MEASURED (EL_Swing_Probe.txt, @ES 60 min): a pivot bar is
// AT OR ABOVE the `strength` OLDER bars and STRICTLY ABOVE the `strength`
// NEWER bars -- bars-ago indexing, so the newer bars are the smaller k and
// take el_gt / el_lt, the older el_ge / el_le; confirmation lag exactly
// `strength`; candidate offsets strength..maxBarsBack-1, the neighbourhood
// reaching `strength` bars past the window, so the deepest bar read is
// maxBarsBack - 1 + strength. No early break: every pivot in the window is
// counted, matching the twin. The comparisons carry the 2.22e-12 relational
// tolerance; the low side's tie sense is the mirror of the measured high-side
// rule. No WFSafe_SwingHigh exists, so plain EL governs.
//
// needN CLAMPS swingPointsCleared TO AT LEAST 1, the way SwingPivotTarget
// clamps its pivotIndex: at 0 the test would be vacuously true on every bar,
// including bars with no pivot in the window at all.
//
// marginTicks (default 0) is V02-18's "breaks resistance by many ticks";
// division-first, ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale() computed once into tickSz,
// both per-symbol constants (VERIFIED, one change print per chart, at bar 1).
//
// Not CloseAbovePriorHighestHigh, which uses a FIXED N-bar window ending one
// bar ago rather than a pivot. The pivot level and the N-bar-highest level genuinely
// differ: after a deep pullback the last swing high can sit far below the
// N-bar high, so neither rule is the other at any parameter. Not
// SwingPointUndercut, which asks whether the bar's low traded through the
// opposite pivot.
// Scratch below is declared in localVariables, not at hook scope: the
// generator only prefixes declared locals, so a hook-scope declaration
// is a redefinition when this rule is placed twice in one strategy.
// Every one is fully assigned each bar before it is read.
tickSz = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
pivS = (int)strength;
pivW = (int)maxBarsBack;
needN = (int)swingPointsCleared;
if (needN < 1) needN = 1;
cntHi = 0;
cntLo = 0;
for (int j = pivS; j <= pivW - 1; ++j) {
    bool okHi = true;
    bool okLo = true;
    for (int k = j - pivS; k < j; ++k) {
        if (!el_gt(high[j], high[k])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_lt(low[j], low[k])) okLo = false;
    }
    for (int k = j + 1; k <= j + pivS; ++k) {
        if (!el_ge(high[j], high[k])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_le(low[j], low[k])) okLo = false;
    }
    if (okHi && el_gt(close[0], high[j] + marginTicks * tickSz)) cntHi = cntHi + 1;
    if (okLo && el_lt(close[0], low[j] - marginTicks * tickSz)) cntLo = cntLo + 1;
}
longSig = (cntHi >= needN);
shortSig = (cntLo >= needN);
